### ⚠️ STOP-and-report: the three `Asymptotics` theorems are **unprovable as stated** (missing measurability)
`randDist_tendstoInProb_cdf`, `randQuantile_tendstoInProb`, and `weakConverges_randPairLaw_of_randDist_tendstoInProb` carry **no measurability hypothesis on `T` or the action**, but the proof provably needs one. `Measure.map f μ = 0` when `f` is not `AEMeasurable`, so:
- the pointwise `randDist` integrates `if T(g•x)≤t …` and needs **per‑`g`** measurability of `x ↦ T(g•x)`;
- the measure `randPairLaw` is `(card²)⁻¹ ∑ᵍ∑ᵍ' P.map(x↦(T(g•x),T(g'•x)))` and needs **per‑pair** measurability.

These junk conventions differ, so the link fails without measurability. I proved this is exactly the missing ingredient: the first‑moment identity `integral_randDist_eq_real_randPairLaw` compiles **iff** given `(hT : Measurable T)` and `(hsmul : ∀ g, Measurable (g • ·))` — the very hypotheses the closed `randTest_exact_level` already threads.

**Fix:** add `(hT : ∀ n, Measurable (T n))` + `(hsmul : ∀ n g, Measurable (fun x => g • x))` (or `[∀ n, MeasurableSMul (G n) (𝓧 n)]` + `hT`) to those three signatures. With the two moment identities + portmanteau bridge already landed, the remaining `_of_measurable` proof is routine (Chebyshev via `mul_meas_ge_le_integral_of_nonneg`, atom‑null `R{t}=0` from continuity via `measure_cdf`/`measure_singleton`/`continuousWithinAt_Iio_iff_leftLim_eq`, frontier via `frontier_prod_univ_eq`/`frontier_Iic`).

This single API gap **also blocks every "consequence" theorem downstream** — `randDist_signChange_tendstoInProb`, `randDist_twoSample_tendstoInProb`, `randDist_studentized_tendstoInProb`, `randDist_affine_tendstoInProb` (Slutsky), and the two `randQuantile_*` — because each has a measurable statistic available (from `hψmeas`) but no slot to pass it into the general theorem.

